1
00:00:00,675 --> 00:00:02,705
You wake up able to hear what people

2
00:00:02,725 --> 00:00:03,608
think of you.

3
00:00:03,629 --> 00:00:06,022
By tonight, your best friend will think

4
00:00:06,042 --> 00:00:07,100
<i>“I miss him.”</i>

5
00:00:08,319 --> 00:00:10,526
You'll be sitting right beside her.

6
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:14,492
It starts in the café.

7
00:00:14,635 --> 00:00:15,549
Usual?

8
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:17,693
Then, without moving his lips:

9
00:00:17,897 --> 00:00:20,052
<i>“Please don't tell me that joke again.”</i>

10
00:00:20,688 --> 00:00:22,169
You close your mouth.

11
00:00:22,271 --> 00:00:23,713
He looks relieved.

12
00:00:23,776 --> 00:00:25,065
You've heard him.

13
00:00:25,128 --> 00:00:27,083
Not everything in his head.

14
00:00:27,103 --> 00:00:29,108
Just thoughts about you, when he's close

15
00:00:29,128 --> 00:00:30,318
enough to talk.

16
00:00:30,391 --> 00:00:32,132
There is no mute button.

17
00:00:32,423 --> 00:00:34,545
Your best friend Mira arrives.

18
00:00:34,812 --> 00:00:35,846
Nice hoodie.

19
00:00:35,962 --> 00:00:37,792
<i>“That green makes him look like a traffic”</i>

20
00:00:37,812 --> 00:00:38,401
<i>“light.”</i>

21
00:00:39,237 --> 00:00:40,561
You stare at her.

22
00:00:40,581 --> 00:00:41,865
Then she thinks

23
00:00:41,885 --> 00:00:42,240
<i>“Still.”</i>

24
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:43,385
<i>“He looks happier.”</i>

25
00:00:44,154 --> 00:00:45,179
Two thoughts.

26
00:00:45,219 --> 00:00:46,683
Three seconds apart.

27
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:48,841
You remember the first.

28
00:00:49,677 --> 00:00:52,047
At work, this starts feeling useful.

29
00:00:52,122 --> 00:00:54,500
Your manager asks for an opinion.

30
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:56,280
<i>“Please disagree with me.”</i>

31
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,658
<i>“Someone needs to.”</i>

32
00:00:58,562 --> 00:00:59,742
So you do.

33
00:00:59,933 --> 00:01:01,116
Exactly!

34
00:01:01,344 --> 00:01:03,359
Your colleague glances over.

35
00:01:03,486 --> 00:01:06,016
<i>“He lets the boss finish.”</i>

36
00:01:06,036 --> 00:01:08,066
<i>“Why does he always interrupt me?”</i>

37
00:01:08,889 --> 00:01:11,116
That afternoon, you let her finish.

38
00:01:11,225 --> 00:01:12,644
She smiles too.

39
00:01:12,664 --> 00:01:14,994
By lunch, you have discovered a shortcut

40
00:01:15,014 --> 00:01:16,112
to being liked.

41
00:01:16,208 --> 00:01:18,413
You laugh before the punchline.

42
00:01:18,433 --> 00:01:21,013
Stop telling a story before anyone gets

43
00:01:21,033 --> 00:01:22,138
bored.

44
00:01:22,158 --> 00:01:24,288
Order the cheap dish because your friend

45
00:01:24,308 --> 00:01:26,501
is worried about splitting the bill.

46
00:01:26,541 --> 00:01:28,346
People relax around you.

47
00:01:28,366 --> 00:01:30,579
You keep a little list on a napkin.

48
00:01:30,599 --> 00:01:31,559
Talk less.

49
00:01:31,579 --> 00:01:32,309
Be funnier.

50
00:01:32,329 --> 00:01:33,709
Be more confident.

51
00:01:33,729 --> 00:01:35,571
Don't make everything a joke.

52
00:01:35,686 --> 00:01:37,340
The list gets longer.

53
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:39,918
By six, it has twenty-three rules.

54
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:42,020
On the train, you catch someone looking

55
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:42,840
at you.

56
00:01:42,916 --> 00:01:43,950
<i>“That hoodie”</i>

57
00:01:44,599 --> 00:01:45,910
You straighten it.

58
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:47,958
<i>“my brother had one like that.”</i>

59
00:01:48,849 --> 00:01:50,796
She turns back to the window.

60
00:01:51,235 --> 00:01:53,065
You're already wondering if you should

61
00:01:53,085 --> 00:01:54,035
take it off.

62
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:56,844
At six, Mira texts.

63
00:01:56,864 --> 00:01:57,369
Coffee?

64
00:01:57,389 --> 00:01:58,349
Rough day.

65
00:01:58,393 --> 00:01:59,569
You get there first.

66
00:01:59,589 --> 00:02:00,734
Buy her favourite.

67
00:02:00,754 --> 00:02:02,304
Choose the quiet table.

68
00:02:02,324 --> 00:02:04,200
Rehearse three things to say.

69
00:02:04,346 --> 00:02:06,551
She arrives without her usual yellow

70
00:02:06,571 --> 00:02:07,416
jacket.

71
00:02:07,436 --> 00:02:09,195
You almost ask why.

72
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:11,305
<i>“He's going to ask about the interview.”</i>

73
00:02:12,155 --> 00:02:13,332
So you don't.

74
00:02:13,352 --> 00:02:15,346
You talk about a film instead.

75
00:02:15,464 --> 00:02:17,497
<i>“Please don't make me do small talk.”</i>

76
00:02:18,348 --> 00:02:19,467
You stop.

77
00:02:19,526 --> 00:02:21,556
She fiddles with the cardboard sleeve

78
00:02:21,576 --> 00:02:22,476
on her cup.

79
00:02:22,751 --> 00:02:23,873
<i>“Say something.”</i>

80
00:02:24,646 --> 00:02:25,808
You start.

81
00:02:25,979 --> 00:02:27,076
<i>“Not a joke.”</i>

82
00:02:27,862 --> 00:02:29,429
You swallow the joke.

83
00:02:29,454 --> 00:02:31,584
For the next ten minutes, you choose

84
00:02:31,604 --> 00:02:33,709
every sentence before she can dislike

85
00:02:33,729 --> 00:02:34,179
it.

86
00:02:34,199 --> 00:02:36,405
You agree when she criticises the film

87
00:02:36,425 --> 00:02:37,505
you loved.

88
00:02:37,525 --> 00:02:39,479
Pretend you aren't hungry when she doesn't

89
00:02:39,499 --> 00:02:40,705
want dinner.

90
00:02:40,725 --> 00:02:43,528
Start laughing, then stop halfway through.

91
00:02:43,648 --> 00:02:45,148
Mira watches you.

92
00:02:45,239 --> 00:02:46,255
You okay?

93
00:02:46,419 --> 00:02:47,577
Of course.

94
00:02:47,681 --> 00:02:48,656
You're being really…

95
00:02:48,676 --> 00:02:49,487
careful.

96
00:02:49,695 --> 00:02:51,028
Then you hear it.

97
00:02:51,197 --> 00:02:52,255
<i>“I miss him.”</i>

98
00:02:53,984 --> 00:02:55,402
You look behind you.

99
00:02:56,022 --> 00:02:57,074
Nobody.

100
00:02:57,846 --> 00:02:59,132
She means you.

101
00:02:59,471 --> 00:03:01,380
You're less than a metre away.

102
00:03:01,458 --> 00:03:04,049
Your napkin is covered in instructions.

103
00:03:04,072 --> 00:03:06,077
For the first time today, none of them

104
00:03:06,097 --> 00:03:06,901
helps.

105
00:03:07,062 --> 00:03:08,498
Did something happen?

106
00:03:08,675 --> 00:03:10,903
You could invent the answer she wants.

107
00:03:11,028 --> 00:03:13,108
Instead, you put the napkin between

108
00:03:13,128 --> 00:03:13,619
you.

109
00:03:13,796 --> 00:03:16,151
I've spent all day trying not to annoy

110
00:03:16,171 --> 00:03:17,002
anyone.

111
00:03:17,225 --> 00:03:18,489
She reads it.

112
00:03:18,542 --> 00:03:19,580
Even me?

113
00:03:19,746 --> 00:03:20,763
You nod.

114
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:22,269
Her first thought is

115
00:03:22,289 --> 00:03:23,832
<i>“That sounds exhausting.”</i>

116
00:03:24,664 --> 00:03:25,880
The next is

117
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:27,418
<i>“I wish he'd trusted me.”</i>

118
00:03:28,945 --> 00:03:30,316
That one hurts.

119
00:03:30,755 --> 00:03:32,322
You leave it alone.

120
00:03:32,373 --> 00:03:33,528
I got rejected.

121
00:03:33,548 --> 00:03:34,571
From the course.

122
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:37,412
You start reaching for something reassuring.

123
00:03:37,589 --> 00:03:39,269
<i>“Please don't say everything happens”</i>

124
00:03:39,289 --> 00:03:40,241
<i>“for a reason.”</i>

125
00:03:41,018 --> 00:03:43,332
You put your hand back on the table.

126
00:03:43,559 --> 00:03:45,297
I don't know what to say.

127
00:03:45,317 --> 00:03:45,902
Good.

128
00:03:45,922 --> 00:03:47,502
You can stop looking for it.

129
00:03:48,733 --> 00:03:50,172
You sit together.

130
00:03:50,739 --> 00:03:52,644
The coffee machine hisses.

131
00:03:52,664 --> 00:03:54,336
Someone drops a spoon.

132
00:03:54,356 --> 00:03:56,786
For a few seconds, Mira isn't thinking

133
00:03:56,806 --> 00:03:58,252
about you at all.

134
00:03:59,246 --> 00:03:59,987
Then

135
00:04:00,007 --> 00:04:01,333
<i>“I'm glad he came.”</i>

136
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:03,994
You could tell her you heard.

137
00:04:04,479 --> 00:04:05,466
You don't.

138
00:04:06,194 --> 00:04:08,166
After a while, she looks up.

139
00:04:08,702 --> 00:04:10,006
I'm glad you came.

140
00:04:10,638 --> 00:04:11,757
Me too.

141
00:04:12,915 --> 00:04:14,995
You stay until the chairs go on the

142
00:04:15,015 --> 00:04:15,865
tables.

143
00:04:18,302 --> 00:04:19,788
Would you want to hear it?
